      "id": 1,
      "text": "East Salem was founded in 1844 when Samuel M. Kurtz built the first house on land purchased from Henry Guyer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/east_salem_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early settlers of East Salem were primarily Scot-Irish immigrants seeking refuge from economic hardships and religious persecution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/east_salem_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The early economy of East Salem relied on mixed farming, focusing on grains like corn and wheat in the ridge-and-valley terrain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/east_salem_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A local post office was established in East Salem shortly after 1850, operating in conjunction with a general store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/east_salem_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early commercial activity in East Salem began in 1848 when John Caveny opened the first store in a house basement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/east_salem_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Early industry in the East Salem area included a grist-mill built around 1776 and a distillery operational by 1783.",
